{
  "description": "SASRec encodes interaction histories with item and positional embeddings, causal self-attention, and feed-forward layers. It predicts the next item by scoring candidate embeddings against the sequence representation. Attention selects relevant past interactions, supporting both recent transitions and longer dependencies. Source: [Self-Attentive Sequential Recommendation](https://arxiv.org/html/1808.09781v1).",
  "motivation": "The paper balances the simplicity of short-context Markov models with the expressive history modeling of recurrent networks. Despite the supplied title, standard SASRec is not a dedicated cold-start method: unseen items lack trained ID embeddings, and users with little history provide limited context.",
  "implementation_notes": "Start from RecHarness sasrec_perdataset and retain all four category models and routing. Use preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], and the supplied 200-epoch environment default. Train with shifted next-item targets, sampled-negative binary cross-entropy, and padding masks. Write artifacts beneath the trial directory and ensure the predictor writer reproduces the trained architecture. Preserve DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and the compatibility interface. Select changes using only pinned macro validation HR@10; no improvement has been measured here. SASRec requires no review text, ratings, or simulator traits.",
  "pseudocode": "for category in four_categories:\n    load unchanged training split\n    initialize category-specific SASRec with seed 42\n    for epoch in configured_epochs(default=200):\n        for sequence, positive, negative in training_batches:\n            features = causal_encoder(item_embedding(sequence) + position_embedding)\n            loss = masked_BCE(features, positive, negative)\n            update_parameters(loss)\n    save model, configuration, and item mappings under trial directory\nwrite predictor that routes categories and loads matching models\nhost evaluates with the pinned validation protocol",
  "originality": {
    "score": 2,
    "positive": "The original paper established self-attention as an effective sequential recommendation architecture.",
    "negative": "Reusing SASRec is baseline reproduction; the supplied description proposes no distinct cold-start mechanism. Score reflects originality relative to the requested baseline, on a 1–10 scale."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "Validation can assess category-specific sequence lengths, regularization, and negative sampling. Available item text could support a separately tested cold-start extension.",
    "negative": "Benefits remain hypotheses and must fit the shared 43,200 GPU-second search budget."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 3,
    "positive": "The existing SASRec baseline and diagnostic contract provide a direct implementation starting point.",
    "negative": "Architecture changes require synchronized checkpoint loading, predictor generation, and diagnostic adapters. Higher scores indicate greater difficulty."
  }
}
